 "gaps": [
  "Evidence is thin: no document from her lifetime survives. The biography body is about 4,450 words, below the tier B floor of 5,000, because the notes support no more without padding.",
  "Birth unknown (about 1719–1731) and death unknown (about 1800–1803; one scholarly view 1802). birth_year and death_year are null. The “1790–1806” range appeared only in a search snippet and is not used.",
  "Grebenka (1845) and the 1847 police gazette are known only as quoted by Bulgakovsky (1891); the originals were not read.",
  "Not read: the Orthodox Encyclopedia (Pravenc) article, A. Rakhmanin’s Life (1909), Saitov’s Petersburg Necropolis (1912), the Russkaya Starina 1873 article, the 2007 Life cited by Russian Wikipedia, Bovkalo and Galkin 1988, and most miracle sections of the 2010 Life.",
  "Smolensky church date conflict: 1786–90 (Azbyka.ru calendar, cemetery article; centenary 1 Oct 1890 in Bulgakovsky) against 1794–96 (memorial plate quoted by Russian Wikipedia). Stated in the source note.",
  "Second closing of the chapel: 1960 (cemetery article) or 18 November 1962 (chapel article).",
  "The prophecy that Emperor Paul would die at 47 is only in the 2010 Life and was not checked against his age at death; it is in the miracles list, not the biography.",
  "The funeral in uniform, the marriage length, the dowry, the death without sacraments, Paraskeva’s son, the c. 1820 pilgrimage date, and the sayings Q13–Q17 come only from modern retellings that name no source.",
  "Q7 (“Leave the dead woman alone…”) has no stated occasion in the notes; the biography and teachings present it as her way of speaking of her former self, next to the modern Q17. The fact checker should confirm the occasion in Bulgakovsky.",
  "The Gospel allusion of “birds of heaven” and the one-line gloss of “fool for Christ” are the narrator’s, not from the notes.",
  "Ivan Antonovich is named without identification (the notes give only “Schlusselburg” and 1764).",
  "Gravestone wording differs slightly between Bulgakovsky and Russian Wikipedia; the English follows the notes.",
  "No prayer text saved; the troparion (tone 7) needs a rights-checked source.",
  "No image chosen; icon and portrait candidates are unverified for rights, and the 2017 portrait attribution is disputed."
